# Privacy Policy for YouTube Hook Generator

**Effective date:** June 5, 2026
**Last updated:** June 5, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how YouTube Hook Generator ("we," "our," or "us")
handles information in connection with the YouTube Hook Generator mobile
application (the "App"). By downloading, accessing, or using the App, you agree
to the practices described in this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, please do
not use the App.

This policy applies to the application identified on Google Play as YouTube Hook
Generator (package name: com.nageshwarrao.youtubehook.generator).

## Summary

- The App generates video hooks, intros, and opening lines on your device.
- We do not require you to create an account, and we do not ask for your name,
  email address, or any personal profile information.
- Content you create or save in the App (such as the topics you type and the
  hooks you save) is stored locally on your device.
- The App may display third-party advertisements. Advertising providers may
  collect certain device and usage information to deliver and measure ads. See
  "Advertising" below.

## Information We Collect

**1. Information you provide.**
The App lets you type a video topic and generate, copy, share, and save hooks.
This content is processed and stored locally on your device. We do not transmit
it to us, and we do not operate servers that receive this content.

**2. Information stored on your device.**
The App saves certain data locally so it can function and remember your choices,
including your saved hooks, your most recent topic and tone selections, and your
theme (light/dark) preference. This information stays on your device and is
removed when you uninstall the App or clear its data.

**3. Information collected automatically by advertising and related services.**
The App may include third-party advertising (for example, Google AdMob). When
ads are enabled, these third-party services may automatically collect information
such as:
- A device advertising identifier (for example, the Google Advertising ID)
- Device information (such as device model, operating system version, language,
  and general settings)
- IP address and the coarse/approximate location derived from it
- Information about how you interact with ads and the App
This information is collected directly by the advertising providers in accordance
with their own privacy policies. We do not control, and are not responsible for,
the data practices of these third parties.

## How We Use Information

We use information to:
- Provide and operate the App's core features (generating, copying, sharing, and
  saving hooks)
- Remember your preferences and saved content on your device
- Display, deliver, and measure advertisements (through third-party ad providers)
- Maintain, troubleshoot, and improve the App
- Comply with legal obligations

We do not sell the content you create in the App.

## Advertising

The App may display advertisements served by third-party advertising networks,
including Google AdMob. These networks may use cookies, device identifiers, and
similar technologies to serve ads that are relevant to you and to measure ad
performance.

- How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services:
  https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- Google AdMob: https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543

**Your ad choices.**
You can limit ad personalization or reset your advertising identifier in your
device settings:
- Android: Settings > Google > Ads, where you can opt out of personalized ads or
  reset your advertising ID.

For users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland,
where required, you will be asked for consent before personalized ads are shown,
and you may withdraw or change your choice as described in that consent prompt.

## Permissions

To show ads and load related content, the App may use the Internet permission to
connect to the network. The App does not request access to your contacts, photos,
microphone, camera, or precise GPS location for its core features.

## Sharing of Information

We do not sell your personal information. Information may be shared only as
follows:
- With third-party advertising and service providers that help us operate the App
  and serve ads, as described above
- To comply with applicable laws, regulations, legal processes, or enforceable
  governmental requests
- To protect the rights, property, or safety of our users, the public, or us
- In connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets, in
  which case any information would remain subject to this Privacy Policy

## Data Retention

Content and preferences stored locally remain on your device until you delete
them, clear the App's data, or uninstall the App. Information collected by
third-party advertising providers is retained according to their respective
retention policies.

## Children's Privacy

The App is not directed to children under the age of 13 (or the minimum age
required in your jurisdiction), and we do not knowingly collect personal
information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal
information, please contact us so we can take appropriate action. Advertisements
shown in the App are intended for a general audience.

## Your Rights

Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal
information, such as the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict its
processing, and the right to object to certain processing or withdraw consent.
- Most content you create in the App is stored only on your device and can be
  deleted by you at any time within the App or by clearing the App's data.
- For requests relating to information handled by third-party advertising
  providers, please also review their privacy policies and opt-out tools linked
  above.
- To exercise any applicable rights with us, contact us using the details below.

**California residents (CCPA/CPRA):** We do not sell your personal information for
money. You have the right to know, delete, and opt out of certain sharing of
personal information, and you will not be discriminated against for exercising
these rights.

**EEA/UK residents (GDPR):** Where we or our partners process personal data, the
legal bases include your consent (for personalized advertising) and legitimate
interests (for operating and securing the App and showing non-personalized ads).
You may withdraw consent at any time.

## Data Security

We take reasonable measures to protect information. Because most data stays on
your device, your device's own security settings (such as a screen lock and
up-to-date software) help protect it. No method of transmission or electronic
storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## International Users

The App may be used worldwide. Third-party providers, such as advertising
networks, may process information in countries other than your own, where data
protection laws may differ. Where required, appropriate safeguards are applied by
those providers.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise
the "Last updated" date above and, where appropriate, provide additional notice.
Your continued use of the App after changes become effective constitutes
acceptance of the revised policy.

